{"id": "en_quake_home_p1", "total": 68.51, "segments": [{"text": "If your house starts shaking violently tonight, do not run outside into the dark street.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.0}, {"text": "Mark relaxes in his living room when a violent tremor strikes right at 2 AM.", "start": 4.74, "end": 7.926}, {"text": "The floor violently rolls, and cracking sounds echo across the shaking two story suburban home.", "start": 8.6, "end": 12.78}, {"text": "Mark wants to bolt outside, but fleeing during violent shaking causes severe crushing trauma injuries.", "start": 13.52, "end": 17.58}, {"text": "Falling bricks, shattered window glass, and exterior building debris injure most people running outside doors.", "start": 18.2, "end": 22.44}, {"text": "One. Drop down low onto your hands and knees before the violent motion throws you.", "start": 23.24, "end": 26.82}, {"text": "Two. Stay away from wide windows, heavy mirrors, and tall furniture that could tip over.", "start": 26.82, "end": 31.12}, {"text": "Cover your vulnerable head and neck beneath a very sturdy table inside the central room.", "start": 31.52, "end": 34.88}, {"text": "Three. Hold on firmly to the heavy table legs with both hands during the shaking.", "start": 35.42, "end": 38.96}, {"text": "Mark shields his neck tightly as picture frames crash loudly to the hardwood living floor.", "start": 39.82, "end": 43.02}, {"text": "After 40 intense seconds, the violent ground rolling finally slows and the house goes quiet.", "start": 43.68, "end": 47.86}, {"text": "He stays alert, knowing that powerful aftershocks often strike homes right after the initial quake.", "start": 48.4, "end": 52.08}, {"text": "Mark carefully crawls out from under the table to check his immediate surroundings for hazards.", "start": 52.7, "end": 55.82}, {"text": "Mark executed the perfect plan, but now there was just one terrifying and deadly problem.", "start": 56.46, "end": 60.74}, {"text": "A sickening rotten egg smell fills the dark room, sig